** (every 2 days; ≈ 1.2 and 1.14): a little more safety stock and a little more waste. Still fits in the 220-unit store. Strong.\n- **1** (every 3 days, ≈ 1.15): fewer order days saves about 84 in fees compared with every-2-day plans. But the day-9 item-1 order (165) covers days 13–15, which need about 195 (including the 103 spike on day 15). Some large deliveries may also be lost because the store is full.\n- **0** (orders every day, ≈ 1.15): good quantities, but 28 order days cost about 294 more in fees than the every-2-day plans.\n- **3** (≈ 1.0 × forecast): no safety margin while demand runs about 4.6% above forecast, so shortages are frequent and expensive.\n- **5** (item 1 ≈ 1.3): too much item 1, so roughly 17 units are wasted every two days.\n- **6** (≈ 1.35 and 1.26): even more waste, and both products arrive on the same days, so part of the item-1 delivery is likely lost when the store is full.\n- **2** (every 4 days, item 1 capped at 170): runs short in the heavy-demand stretches (days 12–15 need about 232). With 4-day shelf life on a 4-day cycle, leftover item 0 spoils. Likely worst.\n\n**Probabilities of being in the top half:** 7: 0.80, 4: 0.75, 1: 0.50, 0: 0.45, 3: 0.40, 5: 0.40, 6: 0.20, 2: 0.10."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5058, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5058}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:35:56.490Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWDo8y7SJiyj4gShfrsM"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": 